From: Codex <codex@local>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: expose existing per-link TX feedback

On the Airoha build iw station statistics expose only the default WCID's
retry/failure counters. Extend the existing read-only per-link queue output
with TXS report totals and TXFREE counters already maintained by the driver.
TXS reports are sampled feedback, not successful-packet counts. TXFREE failed
attempts include retries as well as the terminal status bit. Snapshots are
not coherent across counters. No TX path, MCU queries or counter writers change.

Index: mt76-2026.10.08~639e1287/mt7996/debugfs.c
===================================================================
--- mt76-2026.10.08~639e1287.orig/mt7996/debugfs.c
+++ mt76-2026.10.08~639e1287/mt7996/debugfs.c
@@ -795,6 +795,7 @@ mt7996_sta_hw_queue_read(void *data, str
 		unsigned int cr;
 		u16 wlan_idx;
 		u8 ac;
+		u64 txs = 0;
 
 		mlink = rcu_dereference(mvif->mt76.link[link_id]);
 		if (!mlink)
@@ -809,6 +810,14 @@ mt7996_sta_hw_queue_read(void *data, str
 			   READ_ONCE(msta_link->wcid.link_valid),
 			   test_bit(MT_WCID_FLAG_PS, &msta_link->wcid.flags));
 
+		/* TXS reports are sampled status, not delivered MPDU counts. */
+		for (ac = 0; ac < ARRAY_SIZE(msta_link->wcid.stats.tx_mode); ac++)
+			txs += READ_ONCE(msta_link->wcid.stats.tx_mode[ac]);
+		seq_printf(s, "\t\ttxs_reports:%llu txfree_retries:%u txfree_failed_attempts:%u\n",
+			   (unsigned long long)txs,
+			   READ_ONCE(msta_link->wcid.stats.tx_retries),
+			   READ_ONCE(msta_link->wcid.stats.tx_failed));
+
 		phy = mt7996_vif_link_phy(container_of(mlink,
 						       struct mt7996_vif_link,
 						       mt76));
